==English==

===Verb===
<!--transitive-->
{{en-verb|punches out|punching out|punched out|punched out}}

# {{cx|transitive}} To repeatedly hit a person
# To hit so they become unconscious (knocked out)
#:''I'm going to '''punch out''' that SOB and leave him laying on the ground bleeding.''
# {{cx|transitive}} To use a [[punch]] to remove a piece of material or to remove a piece already [[scored]].
#:''I spent all day '''punching out''' the die cut decals.
# {{context|intransitive|lang=en}} To leave a workplace by punching a [[timecard]]
#: ''I'm going to '''punch out''' a bit early today.''
# {{context|intransitive|lang=en}} To leave a workplace
# {{cx|intransitive}} To eject from an airplane.
#:''With the engine on fire he had to '''punch out''' and hit the silk.''
# {{context|transitive|baseball|lang=en}} To rule (by an [[umpire]]) that a pitch is a called third strike, often done emphatically.
#: ''The ump '''punched out''' the batter with relish to close out the game.''
# {{context|transitive|baseball|lang=en}} To throw a called third [[strike]].
#: ''Jones '''punched out''' the batter to start in the sixth.''

====Antonyms====
{{sense|leave a workplace}} [[punch in]]

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|baseball|lang=en}} An instance of a called third strike.
#: ''Jones' '''punch out''' happened with the bases juiced.''

